window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-1268c961dc837704"]={"key":"ny_main-1268c961dc837704","group":"ny_main","uid":"1268c961dc837704","rank":54,"title":"redcliffe cyber budget compliance 2028","occupation":"financial_managers","archetype":"supplied_source","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are Hedda Ferreira, finance manager at Redcliffe Manufacturing, preparing a client-facing decision pack for Sandpiper Advisory. On 6 October 2028, publication of Redcliffe’s enterprise cyber-insurance budget is paused because the completed workbook contains conflicting United Kingdom allocation figures, and Mirela Ellingsen needs a defensible review before Cormac Tanaka recommends a funding option to the board. Please work offline from `redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx`, `uk_policy_basis_2028.docx`, `uk_cyber_rate_card_2028.xlsx`, `redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx`, and `sandpiper_funding_options.docx`, using the evidence in those files for the position applicable on 30 September 2028. Return two files in the top level of the working directory where you start, using exactly the filenames `Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx` and `Redcliffe_cyber_compliance_assessment.docx`. Do not put either file in a subfolder and do not overwrite the supplied references. The workbook should be corrected rather than merely annotated. (1) Create a public-facing `Budget Review` sheet showing the accepted United Kingdom coverage lines, the applicable coverage layer, resolved transaction date, accepted premium, United Kingdom tax or charge treatment, and line and total amounts in pounds sterling. Make the aggregation traceable to the supplied records and do not collapse separate coverage layers merely because their dates or entity identifiers overlap. (2) Reconcile the conflicting figures using the precedence basis in the supplied policy evidence, and state the selected basis in a `Method & Sources` sheet. The explanation must identify how the business key was applied, how entity identifiers and dates were normalised or resolved, how overlapping rows were distinguished from duplicate premiums, and how row-level notes affected the result. (3) Add a `Defect Log` sheet that records each material quality issue found in the draft, its affected record or field, the impact on the budget, the correction or disposition, and whether the evidence supports the disposition or leaves an assumption. Include issues that are corrected, excluded, retained as separate layers, or deliberately left without a value. (4) Add a `Funding Options` sheet comparing every option in `sandpiper_funding_options.docx`, including the resulting United Kingdom budget, incremental cost or saving, capacity or coverage consequence, and compliance status. Identify one option for approval and give a concise evidence-based reason rather than presenting an unexplained preference. (5) Keep the workbook suitable for an external reader: use clear labels, consistent currency presentation, readable dates, visible source references, and no internal shorthand that is not explained. Do not use the retired helper calculation as evidence, do not silently replace an unsupported value with an estimate, and do not conceal an unresolved interpretation. (6) In the Word assessment, use the exact headings `Executive Recommendation`, `Scope and Evidence`, `Reconciliation`, `Quality Issues`, `Funding Options`, and `Assumptions and Limitations`. Summarise the recommendation, the corrected United Kingdom total, the principal defects, the precedence decision, and the reason the selected option satisfies the supplied requirements. The figures, option names, recommendation, terminology, and scope in the assessment must agree with the workbook. Keep the assessment to five pages or fewer, write for Redcliffe’s external decision maker, and describe the supplied policy evidence as the basis of the conclusion rather than citing internet sources. Both deliverables must be complete, internally consistent, and free of spreadsheet error values such as `#REF!`, `#DIV/0!`, and `#VALUE!`.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx` — Completed but unreviewed cyber-insurance budget workbook containing the transaction register, embedded draft calculations, and the source evidence referenced by the finance team.\n- `references/uk_policy_basis_2028.docx` — Internal policy and governance note stating the applicable United Kingdom review scope, evidence precedence, business key, treatment of approved row exceptions, and presentation requirements.\n- `references/uk_cyber_rate_card_2028.xlsx` — Frozen United Kingdom cyber-insurance rate-card snapshot applicable to the stated as-of date, including layer, limit-band, premium, and tax or charge information.\n- `references/redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx` — Executed coverage schedule and endorsement evidence identifying Redcliffe entities, policy periods, coverage layers, United Kingdom applicability, and authoritative endorsed amounts.\n- `references/sandpiper_funding_options.docx` — Funding-option brief from Sandpiper Advisory listing the available options, costs, capacity, constraints, and United Kingdom compliance conditions.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx` — Corrected, public-facing cyber-insurance budget workbook with reconciled United Kingdom figures, defect log, method and sources, and funding-option comparison. (Write the file at the top level of the starting working directory.; Include sheets named Budget Review, Defect Log, Method & Sources, and Funding Options.; Show traceable source references and retain no spreadsheet error values.; Do not use the retired helper column as a calculation basis.)\n- `Redcliffe_cyber_compliance_assessment.docx` — External-facing compliance assessment explaining the reconciliation, quality issues, funding comparison, recommendation, and limitations. (Write the file at the top level of the starting working directory.; Use the headings Executive Recommendation, Scope and Evidence, Reconciliation, Quality Issues, Funding Options, and Assumptions and Limitations.; Keep the document to five pages or fewer.; All shared figures and conclusions must agree with the workbook.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx","bytes":38828,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/5446cc6104479aea61e70f852e5e8e5080d44a6e770ccdb6101842e5d993cb21.docx","sha256":"5446cc6104479aea61e70f852e5e8e5080d44a6e770ccdb6101842e5d993cb21","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Cyber Insurance 2028 - Executed Coverage Schedule\nPolicy RCL-CY-2028 | Executed extract for the September budget review\nPolicyholder\nRedcliffe Manufacturing plc\nPolicy period\n01 Jan 2028 - 31 Dec 2028\nIssued\n18 September 2028\n\nThe following schedule lines identify the insured entity, territory, coverage layer and executed premium. All dates below are calendar dates.\nEntity ID\nInsured entity\nTerritory\nLayer\nLimit\nEffective / transaction date\nExecuted premium\nStatus\nRM-UK-01\nRedcliffe Manufacturing plc\nUnited Kingdom\nL1\n£10m\n30 September 2028\n£84,000.00\nExecuted\nRM-UK-01\nRedcliffe Manufacturing plc\nUnited Kingdom\nL2\n£5m\n30 September 2028\n£52,500.00\nExecuted\nRM-UK-02\nRedcliffe Components Ltd\nUnited Kingdom\nL1\n£5m\n10 September 2028\n£41,250.00\nExecuted\nRM-UK-03\nRedcliffe Digital Services Ltd\nUnited Kingdom\nL1\n£2m\n30 September 2028\n£31,800.00\nExecuted\nRM-UK-04\nRedcliffe Distribution Ltd\nUnited Kingdom\nL3\n£2m\n30 September 2028\n£24,900.00\nExecuted\nRM-UK-05\nRedcliffe Engineering Ltd\nUnited Kingdom\nL2\n£3m\n30 September 2028\n£28,600.00\nCancelled by EN-19\nRM-US-01\nRedcliffe Systems Inc.\nUnited States\nL1\n£10m\n30 September 2028\n£62,000.00\nExecuted\nApproved endorsements and riders\nReference\nDate\nApplies to\nExecuted instruction\nEN-14\n26 Sep 2028\nRM-UK-01 | L1 | 2028\nPremium amended from £84,000.00 to £86,500.00, effective 30 September 2028.\nEN-19\n28 Sep 2028\nRM-UK-05 | L2 | 2028\nCancelled effective 30 September 2028. The line is not to be included in the United Kingdom budget.\nRider CH-3\n18 Sep 2028\nRM-UK-03 | L1 | 2028\nUnited Kingdom charge is not applicable. Present the charge field as blank.\nThis schedule is the authoritative record for executed coverage and endorsed amendments. Execution note: The RM-UK-02 L1 line is dated 10 September 2028.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx","bytes":7129,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/48844b971fa271bfd43af16238b9e0e05c090be21f3224e327166045617fad02.xlsx","sha256":"48844b971fa271bfd43af16238b9e0e05c090be21f3224e327166045617fad02","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Budget Register","row_count":12,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Redcliffe Manufacturing plc - Enterprise Cyber Budget"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Budget status","Rev 5 - publication hold","","Draft UK total (unreviewed)","=SUMIF($D$8:$D$15,\"United Kingdom\",$K$8:$K$15)  [缓存: 缺失]","","Prepared by","Finance Planning"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Programme: RCL-CY-2028 | Exported 05 Oct 2028 16:42 GMT | Currency: GBP"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Record ID","Entity ID","Insured entity","Territory","Coverage layer","Policy year","Transaction date","Limit band","Draft premium (£)","Draft UK charge (£)","Draft line total (£)","Retired Helper Calc (£)","Source batch","Notes"]},{"r":"8","cells":["TR-1001","RM-UK-01","Redcliffe Manufacturing plc","United Kingdom","L1","2028","47026","£10m","80000","9600","=I8+J8  [缓存: 缺失]","92720","CYB-SEP-A","Approved endorsement EN-14: premium set to £86,500.00."]},{"r":"9","cells":["TR-1002","RM-UK-01 ","Redcliffe Manufacturing plc","United Kingdom","L2","2028","30/09/2028","£5m","52500","6300","=I9+J9  [缓存: 缺失]","58590","CYB-SEP-A",""]},{"r":"10","cells":["TR-1003","rm-uk-02","Redcliffe Components Ltd","United Kingdom","L1","2028","09/10/2028","£5m","39000","4680","=I10+J10  [缓存: 缺失]","43680","CYB-SEP-B",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["TR-1004"," RM-UK-02 ","Redcliffe Components Ltd","United Kingdom","L1","2028","47006.60416666666","£5m","39000","4680","=I11+J11  [缓存: 缺失]","41184","CYB-SEP-C",""]},{"r":"12","cells":["TR-1005","RM-UK-03","Redcliffe Digital Services Ltd","United Kingdom","L1","2028","2028-09-30","£2m","30000","0","=I12+J12  [缓存: 缺失]","35616","CYB-SEP-A","Approved rider CH-3: UK charge not applicable for this line."]},{"r":"13","cells":["TR-1006","RM-UK-04","Redcliffe Distribution Ltd","United Kingdom","L3","2028","2028-09-30T00:00:00","£2m","23000","2760","=I13+J13  [缓存: 缺失]","27600","CYB-SEP-A",""]},{"r":"14","cells":["TR-1007","RM-UK-05","Redcliffe Engineering Ltd","United Kingdom","L2","2028","30/09/2028","£3m","28600","3432","=I14+J14  [缓存: 缺失]","31920","CYB-SEP-A","Cancelled under EN-19 effective 30 September 2028; do not include in UK budget."]},{"r":"15","cells":["TR-1008","RM-US-01","Redcliffe Systems Inc.","United States","L1","2028","47026","£10m","62000","7440","=I15+J15  [缓存: 缺失]","69440","CYB-SEP-US",""]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/sandpiper_funding_options.docx","bytes":38560,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/c1a9028d38e523d51d1b0b90cf912d7759de3a017714ba39a2043038382f822e.docx","sha256":"c1a9028d38e523d51d1b0b90cf912d7759de3a017714ba39a2043038382f822e","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Funding Route Options for the UK Cyber Programme\nSandpiper Advisory | Decision brief prepared 03 October 2028\nClient\nRedcliffe Manufacturing plc\nDecision date\n06 October 2028\nCurrency\nGBP\n\nUnited Kingdom conditions\nA route is compliant only when all of the following conditions are met as at 30 September 2028:\nFunding capacity must be at least the corrected United Kingdom insurance budget, before the funding fee.\nThe route must be available by 30 September 2028 and preserve every schedule-backed United Kingdom coverage line.\nA ring-fenced contingency reserve of at least £15,000 must be maintained for the programme.\nEach funding fee is charged in addition to the corrected insurance budget. Capacity is measured against the insurance budget before that fee.\nAvailable funding routes\nOption\nFunding fee\nCapacity\nAvailability\nCoverage consequence\nRing-fenced reserve\nTreasury Cash Release\n£0.00\n£300,000.00\n30 Sep 2028\nNo coverage change\n£0.00\nSandpiper Managed Premium Facility\n£6,250.00\n£300,000.00\n30 Sep 2028\nNo coverage change\n£20,000.00\nCollateralised Reserve Facility\n£9,800.00\n£350,000.00\n30 Sep 2028\nNo coverage change\n£25,000.00\nDecision note\nTreasury Cash Release has no funding fee but does not establish the required ring-fenced contingency reserve and is therefore not compliant. Both facility routes preserve the coverage and meet the capacity, timing and reserve conditions. The final recommendation should use the corrected budget from the review and compare the resulting total cost.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/uk_cyber_rate_card_2028.xlsx","bytes":6382,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/d75f0d8a645713d3f7615fe2dae2bb4801313531839425f0fd9853783ee564a4.xlsx","sha256":"d75f0d8a645713d3f7615fe2dae2bb4801313531839425f0fd9853783ee564a4","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"UK Rate Card","row_count":11,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["United Kingdom Cyber Rate Card - Frozen Snapshot"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Snapshot ID","FRZ-RCL-UK-2028-09","","Effective period","01 Jan 2028 to 31 Dec 2028","","Currency","GBP"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Frozen for the September review; values are not a live quotation."]},{"r":"7","cells":["Rate card ID","Effective from","Effective to","Coverage layer","Limit band","Base premium (£)","UK charge rate","UK charge treatment","Rate note"]},{"r":"8","cells":["RC-28-L1-10","46753","47118","L1","£10m","84000","0.12","Standard","Schedule endorsement may amend premium."]},{"r":"9","cells":["RC-28-L2-05","46753","47118","L2","£5m","52500","0.12","Standard",""]},{"r":"10","cells":["RC-28-L1-05","46753","47118","L1","£5m","41250","0.12","Standard",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["RC-28-L1-02","46753","47118","L1","£2m","31800","0.12","Blank where approved schedule rider says not applicable","Rider evidence controls treatment."]},{"r":"12","cells":["RC-28-L3-02","46753","47118","L3","£2m","24900","0.12","Standard",""]},{"r":"13","cells":["RC-28-L2-03","46753","47118","L2","£3m","28600","0.12","Standard",""]},{"r":"15","cells":["Charge note","Apply the stated rate to the accepted premium. Where an approved schedule rider says the UK charge is not applicable, leave the charge field blank."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/uk_policy_basis_2028.docx","bytes":38831,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/16d1d0cf40a6456191e8315e61b74049174b56869266f1917eff932db13309b7.docx","sha256":"16d1d0cf40a6456191e8315e61b74049174b56869266f1917eff932db13309b7","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"United Kingdom Cyber Budget Review Basis\nInternal governance note | Version 1.2 | Issued 26 September 2028\nOwner\nFinance Risk & Controls\nProgramme\nRCL-CY-2028\nApplies as at\n30 September 2028\n\nReview scope\nThis review covers United Kingdom policy costs applicable on 30 September 2028. It is a budget and evidence review only. The conclusion must not extend beyond the supplied United Kingdom policy text, executed schedule, frozen rate-card snapshot and funding brief.\nReconciliation rules\nUse the business key: normalised entity identifier, coverage layer, policy year and resolved transaction date.\nNormalise entity identifiers by trimming surrounding whitespace and matching without regard to case before grouping or de-duplication.\nDistinct coverage layers are separate premiums even where an entity and resolved date overlap. Remove only records whose full business key matches.\nCarry unambiguous dates through to a calendar date. Resolve an ambiguous slash-form date only where the executed coverage schedule corroborates the result, and disclose the treatment.\nEvidence precedence is: executed coverage schedule and approved endorsement evidence; then frozen rate card; then draft workbook figures. The Retired Helper Calc is non-authoritative and must not determine an accepted line amount, UK charge or total.\nAn approved exception in Notes overrides only the named field or disposition. It does not displace otherwise applicable schedule, rate-card or scope evidence.\nCalculate a UK charge from the frozen rate card on the accepted premium unless an approved exception says it is not applicable. In that case leave the UK charge field blank; do not use zero or an estimate.\nRequired compliance statement\nThe assessment must state a supported conclusion for each of the following United Kingdom review controls:\nUnited Kingdom scope and the 30 September 2028 as-of date.\nNormalised business-key de-duplication and retention of distinct layers.\nEvidence precedence, date corroboration and approved Notes exceptions.\nFrozen rate-card applicability and the UK charge treatment, including any blank exception.\nFunding route compliance with every United Kingdom condition stated in Sandpiper Advisory's supplied funding brief.\nPresentation must show the selected evidence basis, source references and any limitation or assumption. Do not describe a requirement as compliant unless the supplied evidence supports it.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx","bytes":19856,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/66d1acda32cc5a0fe99b2e1cb2ae8e598b639812f2ab4eefc913293915a9052c.xlsx","sha256":"66d1acda32cc5a0fe99b2e1cb2ae8e598b639812f2ab4eefc913293915a9052c","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Budget Review","row_count":12,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Redcliffe Manufacturing plc | Cyber Insurance Budget Review","","","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Prepared for Sandpiper Advisory | United Kingdom policy costs applicable on 30 September 2028 | Currency: GBP","","","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"4","cells":["Accepted premium","236950","","","Applicable UK charge","24618","","","Corrected UK budget","261568","","","Review status","Reconciled"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Accepted values follow executed schedule and approved endorsements, then the frozen rate card. The retired helper calculation is excluded from this review.","","","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["Source record","Normalised entity ID","Insured entity","Applicable coverage layer","Limit band","Policy year","Resolved transaction date","Accepted premium (£)","United Kingdom charge treatment","UK charge rate","UK charge (£)","Line amount (£)","Source references","Reconciliation note"]},{"r":"8","cells":["TR-1001","RM-UK-01","Redcliffe Manufacturing plc","L1","£10m","2028","47026","86500","Standard UK charge at 12.00%","0.12","10380","96880","Draft TR-1001; Schedule RM-UK-01/L1; Rate card RC-28-L1-10; EN-14","EN-14 premium override applied; iso/date-time carried to calendar date"]},{"r":"9","cells":["TR-1002","RM-UK-01","Redcliffe Manufacturing plc","L2","£5m","2028","47026","52500","Standard UK charge at 12.00%","0.12","6300","58800","Draft TR-1002; Schedule RM-UK-01/L2; Rate card RC-28-L2-05","Unambiguous day-first slash date"]},{"r":"10","cells":["TR-1003","RM-UK-02","Redcliffe Components Ltd","L1","£5m","2028","47006","41250","Standard UK charge at 12.00%","0.12","4950","46200","Draft TR-1003; Schedule RM-UK-02/L1; Rate card RC-28-L1-05","Ambiguous slash date resolved to executed schedule date"]},{"r":"11","cells":["TR-1005","RM-UK-03","Redcliffe Digital Services Ltd","L1","£2m","2028","47026","31800","Not applicable - blank per Rider CH-3","N/A","","31800","Draft TR-1005; Schedule RM-UK-03/L1; Rate card RC-28-L1-02; Rider CH-3","Rider CH-3 makes UK charge not applicable; charge left blank"]},{"r":"12","cells":["TR-1006","RM-UK-04","Redcliffe Distribution Ltd","L3","£2m","2028","47026","24900","Standard UK charge at 12.00%","0.12","2988","27888","Draft TR-1006; Schedule RM-UK-04/L3; Rate card RC-28-L3-02","ISO/date-time carried to calendar date"]},{"r":"13","cells":["United Kingdom total","","","","","","","=SUM(H8:H12)  [缓存: 236950]","","","=SUM(K8:K12)  [缓存: 24618]","=SUM(L8:L12)  [缓存: 261568]","",""]},{"r":"16","cells":["Decision-ready result: five schedule-backed United Kingdom coverage lines have been accepted. The applicable UK budget is shown above; the funding recommendation is on the Funding Options sheet.","","","","","","","","","","","","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Funding Options","row_count":9,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Funding Options","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Comparison of every route supplied by Sandpiper Advisory against the corrected United Kingdom insurance budget","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"4","cells":["Corrected UK insurance budget before funding fee","261568","","Funding-brief reserve threshold","15000","","Approval recommendation","Sandpiper Managed Premium Facility","","",""]},{"r":"6","cells":["Option","Funding capacity (£)","Available by","Coverage consequence","Ring-fenced reserve (£)","Corrected UK budget (£)","Funding fee (£)","Resulting UK cost (£)","Incremental cost / (saving) (£)","United Kingdom compliance status","Evidence-based comparison"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Treasury Cash Release","300000","30 Sep 2028","No coverage change","0","261568","0","261568","0","Not compliant","ring-fenced reserve below £15,000.00"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Sandpiper Managed Premium Facility","300000","30 Sep 2028","No coverage change","20000","261568","6250","267818","6250","Compliant - recommended for approval","All conditions met; £3,550.00 lower total cost than the other compliant route."]},{"r":"9","cells":["Collateralised Reserve Facility","350000","30 Sep 2028","No coverage change","25000","261568","9800","271368","9800","Compliant","All funding-brief conditions met"]},{"r":"12","cells":["Recommendation: approve Sandpiper Managed Premium Facility at £267,818.00 total UK cost (corrected budget £261,568.00 plus £6,250.00 fee). It funds the full corrected budget, preserves all schedule-backed coverage, is available by 30 September 2028, maintains a £20,000.00 ring-fenced reserve, and costs £3,550.00 less than the other compliant route.","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"14","cells":["Source: sandpiper_funding_options.docx, United Kingdom conditions and Available funding routes. Capacity is assessed before the funding fee, as specified in the supplied brief.","","","","","","","","","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Defect Log","row_count":13,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Defect Log","","","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Material quality issues identified in the unreviewed draft and their evidence-backed disposition","","","","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["Issue ID","Quality issue","Affected record or field","Budget / compliance impact","Correction or disposition","Evidence status and source"]},{"r":"6","cells":["QA-01","Mixed transaction-date representations","Transaction date field: ISO date, ISO date-time, day-first slash and slash-form values across TR-1001 to TR-1008.","Could split matching records or misstate the transaction date used in the business key.","Converted each supported value to a calendar date before key construction; time was not retained in the key.","Supported - uk_policy_basis_2028.docx, Reconciliation rules; redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx, Budget Register. No assumption."]},{"r":"7","cells":["QA-02","Ambiguous slash-form date","TR-1003 transaction date 09/10/2028.","Could be 09 Oct or 10 Sep, affecting grouping and eligibility.","Resolved as 10 Sep 2028 because RM-UK-02/L1 is uniquely dated 10 September 2028 in the executed schedule.","Supported - redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx, RM-UK-02/L1. No assumption."]},{"r":"8","cells":["QA-03","Case and surrounding whitespace in entity identifiers","TR-1002, TR-1003 and TR-1004 Entity ID values.","Could prevent matching or allow duplicate premiums into the budget.","Trimmed surrounding whitespace and matched case-insensitively before grouping. The schedule form is displayed.","Supported - uk_policy_basis_2028.docx, Reconciliation rules; draft records. No assumption."]},{"r":"9","cells":["QA-04","Same-key duplicate import","TR-1004 duplicates TR-1003 after identifier and date resolution.","Including both would overstate the budget by £46,200.00.","Excluded TR-1004; retained TR-1003 as the schedule-backed line.","Supported - business-key rule in uk_policy_basis_2028.docx and RM-UK-02/L1 schedule evidence. No assumption."]},{"r":"10","cells":["QA-05","Overlapping records are separate coverage layers","TR-1001 L1 and TR-1002 L2 both resolve to RM-UK-01 on 30 Sep 2028.","Dropping one on date or entity overlap would understate schedule-backed coverage and cost.","Retained L1 and L2 as separate premiums because coverage layer is part of the business key.","Supported - uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx, RM-UK-01 L1 and L2. No assumption."]},{"r":"11","cells":["QA-06","Approved premium exception in Notes","TR-1001 Notes and Draft premium (£).","Draft line £89,600.00 conflicts with the endorsed line £96,880.00.","Applied only the EN-14 premium override of £86,500.00 and then calculated the standard UK charge on that accepted premium.","Supported - TR-1001 Notes; executed EN-14. No assumption."]},{"r":"12","cells":["QA-07","Approved UK-charge exception in Notes","TR-1005 Notes and United Kingdom charge field.","A zero or estimated charge would contradict the approved rider and distort disclosure.","Accepted the premium, left the UK charge cell blank and retained line amount at the premium only.","Supported - TR-1005 Notes; Rider CH-3. No assumption."]},{"r":"13","cells":["QA-08","Cancellation instruction in Notes","TR-1007 Notes and drafted amounts.","Including the cancelled line would overstate the United Kingdom budget by £32,032.00 on the draft fields.","Excluded the line from all United Kingdom totals under EN-19.","Supported - TR-1007 Notes; executed EN-19. No assumption."]},{"r":"14","cells":["QA-09","Stale retired helper calculation","Retired Helper Calc (£) column for the full draft register.","Helper values disagree with schedule, endorsement and rate evidence and could propagate a stale total.","Marked non-authoritative and did not use the column in any accepted premium, charge, line amount or total.","Supported - uk_policy_basis_2028.docx, Reconciliation rules. No assumption."]},{"r":"15","cells":["QA-10","Out-of-scope programme row","TR-1008 territory: United States.","A non-United Kingdom line would overstate the United Kingdom budget and extend the conclusion beyond scope.","Excluded from United Kingdom review totals; retained in the source trace only.","Supported - policy scope and executed schedule territory. No assumption."]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Method & Sources","row_count":12,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Method & Sources","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["United Kingdom-only review | Evidence applicable on 30 September 2028 | All conclusions are based on supplied records","","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["Review element","Applied basis","Source references","Conclusion / disclosure"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Scope and as-of date","Reviewed United Kingdom policy costs applicable on 30 September 2028 only. United States records are not included in the United Kingdom budget or conclusion.","uk_policy_basis_2028.docx, Review scope; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx, coverage lines","Scope supported; no live market, legal or internet source was used."]},{"r":"7","cells":["Business key","UPPER(TRIM(Entity ID)) + coverage layer + policy year + resolved transaction date. The executed schedule display identifier is used in the review output.","uk_policy_basis_2028.docx, Reconciliation rules; redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx, Budget Register","Entity identifiers were trimmed and matched case-insensitively before grouping or de-duplication."]},{"r":"8","cells":["Date treatment","ISO values and date-times were carried to a calendar date. The unambiguous 30/09/2028 values were treated day-first. Ambiguous 09/10/2028 for TR-1003 was resolved as 10 Sep 2028 only because the executed RM-UK-02/L1 schedule line is uniquely dated 10 September 2028.","redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx, TR-1001 to TR-1008; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx, RM-UK-02/L1","The ambiguous interpretation is disclosed and schedule-corroborated."]},{"r":"9","cells":["Duplicate versus separate layer","TR-1004 has the same normalised business key as TR-1003 and was removed as a duplicate import. RM-UK-01 L1 and L2 share 30 Sep 2028 but remain separate because their coverage layers differ.","redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx, TR-1001 to TR-1004; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx, RM-UK-01 and RM-UK-02 lines","Only the exact-key duplicate was removed; overlapping layers were retained."]},{"r":"10","cells":["Evidence precedence","Executed schedule and approved endorsements were applied first, then the frozen rate card, then draft figures. Retired Helper Calc was not used for any premium, charge or total.","uk_policy_basis_2028.docx, Reconciliation rules; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx, EN-14/EN-19/Rider CH-3; uk_cyber_rate_card_2028.xlsx","Selected basis is supported by the supplied policy evidence."]},{"r":"11","cells":["Approved Notes exceptions","TR-1001 uses EN-14's £86,500.00 premium override only. TR-1005 keeps the UK charge field blank under Rider CH-3. TR-1007 is excluded under EN-19.","redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx, Notes; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx, EN-14, EN-19 and Rider CH-3","Each exception changed only its named field or disposition."]},{"r":"12","cells":["Premium and UK charge calculation","Rate-card rows effective 01 Jan to 31 Dec 2028 validate each layer and limit band. Standard charge is 12.00% of accepted premium; Rider CH-3 is presented as blank rather than zero.","uk_cyber_rate_card_2028.xlsx, UK Rate Card RC-28-L1-10 to RC-28-L3-02; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx, Rider CH-3","Accepted premium £236,950.00; applicable UK charge £24,618.00; corrected UK budget £261,568.00."]},{"r":"13","cells":["United Kingdom compliance conclusion","The review confirms the stated scope, key, date, precedence, rate-card and charge controls. Funding is assessed against every United Kingdom condition in Sandpiper Advisory's brief.","uk_policy_basis_2028.docx, Required compliance statement; sandpiper_funding_options.docx, United Kingdom conditions","Sandpiper Managed Premium Facility is the lowest-cost compliant supplied funding route."]},{"r":"14","cells":["Layer-code presentation","L1, L2 and L3 are retained as executed schedule coverage-layer identifiers. No unsupplied coverage description has been inferred.","redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx, coverage lines","Source terminology retained for traceability."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/Redcliffe_cyber_compliance_assessment.docx","bytes":39888,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/a15299278ca97b068a12b37305fc5bf7e13f8ceb76a6aab54a5e4c98fe6d20cb.docx","sha256":"a15299278ca97b068a12b37305fc5bf7e13f8ceb76a6aab54a5e4c98fe6d20cb","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Cyber Insurance Budget Compliance Assessment\nRedcliffe Manufacturing plc | Prepared for Sandpiper Advisory | 6 October 2028\nExecutive Recommendation\nApprove the Sandpiper Managed Premium Facility. The corrected United Kingdom insurance budget is £261,568.00, comprising £236,950.00 of accepted premiums and £24,618.00 of applicable United Kingdom charges. The recommended route adds a £6,250.00 funding fee, for a resulting United Kingdom cost of £267,818.00.\nIt is the lowest-cost supplied route that meets every condition in the funding brief: £300,000.00 capacity against the £261,568.00 corrected budget before fee, availability by 30 September 2028, no coverage change and a £20,000.00 ring-fenced contingency reserve.\nScope and Evidence\nThis is a United Kingdom-only review of policy costs applicable on 30 September 2028. The conclusion is based on the supplied draft budget register, United Kingdom policy basis, frozen rate card, executed coverage schedule and Sandpiper Advisory funding brief. The supplied policy basis requires a supported conclusion on scope, normalised business-key reconciliation, evidence precedence and dates, notes-based exceptions, rate-card charges and funding conditions.\nThe executed schedule and approved endorsements were treated as the highest-precedence evidence, followed by the frozen rate card and then the draft workbook. The draft Retired Helper Calc was non-authoritative and was not used in any accepted figure.\nReconciliation\nThe business key used was entity identifier after trimming surrounding whitespace and matching case-insensitively, plus coverage layer, policy year and resolved transaction date. Five schedule-backed United Kingdom coverage lines were accepted. RM-UK-01 L1 and L2 both fall on 30 September 2028 but were retained as separate premiums because the layers differ. TR-1004 was removed because it matches TR-1003 on the full normalised key.\nUnambiguous dates were carried to calendar dates. The ambiguous draft value 09/10/2028 for TR-1003 was resolved as 10 September 2028 only because the executed RM-UK-02 L1 schedule line is uniquely dated 10 September 2028. EN-14 changes the RM-UK-01 L1 premium to £86,500.00; that approved exception overrides the main draft premium only. Standard charges were calculated at 12.00% of accepted premium. Rider CH-3 makes the RM-UK-03 L1 charge not applicable, so that charge field remains blank.\nAccepted line\nResolved date\nPremium\nUK charge\nLine amount\nRM-UK-01 L1\n30 Sep 2028\n£86,500.00\n£10,380.00\n£96,880.00\nRM-UK-01 L2\n30 Sep 2028\n£52,500.00\n£6,300.00\n£58,800.00\nRM-UK-02 L1\n10 Sep 2028\n£41,250.00\n£4,950.00\n£46,200.00\nRM-UK-03 L1\n30 Sep 2028\n£31,800.00\nBlank - Rider CH-3\n£31,800.00\nRM-UK-04 L3\n30 Sep 2028\n£24,900.00\n£2,988.00\n£27,888.00\nQuality Issues\nThe draft contains mixed date and time representations, including the ambiguous slash-form date; entity identifiers with case and whitespace differences; and a same-key duplicate import. These were resolved using the policy business-key rules and the executed schedule. The log also records the two legitimate layers sharing a date, so they are not mistaken for duplicates.\nThe Notes field contained three approved dispositions. EN-14 corrects the TR-1001 premium; Rider CH-3 requires a blank charge on TR-1005; and EN-19 cancels TR-1007, which is excluded from all United Kingdom totals. The United States row TR-1008 is outside scope. The Retired Helper Calc is stale and excluded. Each correction and exclusion is supported by a supplied record; no unsupported estimate was used.\n\n\nFunding Options\nOption\nResulting UK cost\nIncremental cost\nCapacity\nReserve\nStatus\nTreasury Cash Release\n£261,568.00\n£0.00\n£300,000.00\n£0.00\nNot compliant\nSandpiper Managed Premium Facility\n£267,818.00\n£6,250.00\n£300,000.00\n£20,000.00\nRecommended: compliant\nCollateralised Reserve Facility\n£271,368.00\n£9,800.00\n£350,000.00\n£25,000.00\nCompliant\nTreasury Cash Release is £0.00 incremental cost but is not compliant because it has no ring-fenced reserve. The Collateralised Reserve Facility is compliant at £271,368.00, but costs £3,550.00 more than the recommendation.\nAssumptions and Limitations\nNo unsupported premium, charge, coverage or funding assumption was used. The charge exemption is presented as blank rather than zero, and the ambiguous date treatment is disclosed above. This assessment is limited to the supplied United Kingdom policy evidence and frozen rate-card snapshot applicable on 30 September 2028. It is not a live legal, tax, insurance-market or funding opinion.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted workbook exists as `Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx` with the required `.xlsx` format.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted file set","grader_hint":"Inspect the filename and open the file with an office-library reader."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted assessment exists as `Redcliffe_cyber_compliance_assessment.docx` with the required `.docx` format.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted file set","grader_hint":"Inspect the filename and confirm the document opens as an OOXML Word document."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains sheets named `Budget Review`, `Defect Log`, `Method & Sources`, and `Funding Options`.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx","grader_hint":"Read the workbook sheet-name collection and compare exact names."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Budget Review includes every in-scope United Kingdom coverage line supported by the policy basis and executed coverage schedule, with no accepted line omitted.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx; uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Budget Review","grader_hint":"Build the canonical set from the schedule-backed, United Kingdom-applicable records after applying the supplied scope and key rules, then compare it to the review lines."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Entity identifiers are normalised for comparison by removing surrounding whitespace and applying case-insensitive matching before grouping or de-duplication.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx; uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Method & Sources","grader_hint":"Compare identifiers differing only by case or trailing spaces and inspect both the resulting grouping and the disclosed method."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Duplicate premiums are removed only when the normalised entity identifier, coverage layer, policy year, and resolved transaction date all match the stated business key.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx; uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Budget Review","grader_hint":"Reconstruct the key from the source records and verify that exact-key duplicates contribute once while nonmatching records remain eligible."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Rows representing distinct coverage layers are retained as separate premiums even when their normalised entity and transaction date overlap.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx; uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Budget Review","grader_hint":"Compare layer identifiers in the schedule with the review output; overlapping dates alone must not cause collapse."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Unambiguous dates are carried through correctly, and the ambiguous slash-form date is resolved consistently with the corroborating coverage evidence rather than silently interpreted without support.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Method & Sources","grader_hint":"Compare the date column formats and the matching schedule dates, then confirm the chosen interpretation and its evidence are disclosed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For conflicting figures, the accepted value follows the precedence hierarchy in the supplied policy basis and the selected source is recorded.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx; uk_cyber_rate_card_2028.xlsx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Method & Sources","grader_hint":"For each conflict, compare the workbook result with the hierarchy stated in the policy basis and require a source or record reference."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An approved note exception that overrides a main-column premium is applied to the accepted amount and the override is identified in the method or defect log.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx; uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx","grader_hint":"Locate the approved exception in the source Notes field and compare its stated treatment with the corresponding review line."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A row whose Notes field directs exclusion is not included in any United Kingdom budget total, while the exclusion and reason remain visible in the defect log or source trace.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx; uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Defect Log","grader_hint":"Check the canonical excluded-record set and verify that excluded rows do not contribute to totals."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The field for a United Kingdom charge that the supplied exception identifies as not applicable remains blank, rather than being filled with zero, an estimate, or an invented amount.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx; uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Budget Review","grader_hint":"Find the exception-designated non-applicable line and inspect the charge cell and its accompanying explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The retired helper column is explicitly identified as non-authoritative and does not determine any accepted line amount, tax amount, or total.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx; uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Method & Sources","grader_hint":"Compare output values with the authoritative schedule and rate evidence rather than the retired helper values, and look for an explicit disclosure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Only coverage lines within the United Kingdom review scope are included in the United Kingdom budget and compliance conclusion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx","grader_hint":"Rebuild the in-scope set from the supplied scope fields and check that non-United-Kingdom records are not aggregated."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each accepted premium agrees with the applicable rate-card layer, limit band, policy date, and any supported endorsement, within ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"uk_cyber_rate_card_2028.xlsx; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Budget Review","grader_hint":"Recalculate the premium from the frozen rate-card inputs and schedule-supported adjustments; allow a currency tolerance of ±£1."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The United Kingdom charge shown for each applicable accepted line equals the accepted premium multiplied by the applicable supplied rate, within ±£1; a documented exception is blank where the source says it is not applicable.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"uk_cyber_rate_card_2028.xlsx; uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Budget Review","grader_hint":"Recalculate line charges from the rate-card rate and accepted premium, allowing ±£1, and separately inspect the designated blank exception."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The total accepted United Kingdom premium equals the sum of accepted, non-excluded, de-duplicated coverage lines, within ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx; uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx","grader_hint":"Compute the canonical accepted-line sum independently and compare to the workbook total with ±£1 tolerance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The total applicable United Kingdom charge equals the sum of the line charges that are not blank, within ±£1.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"uk_cyber_rate_card_2028.xlsx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Budget Review","grader_hint":"Sum the applicable line-level charges and compare with the displayed total using ±£1 tolerance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reported United Kingdom budget total equals accepted premium plus applicable United Kingdom charges and any supported cost component required by the supplied policy basis, within ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; uk_cyber_rate_card_2028.xlsx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx","grader_hint":"Recalculate the total from the displayed accepted components and source-supported required costs, allowing ±£1."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every funding option’s total cost and incremental difference are calculated from the corrected budget and option terms, within ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"sandpiper_funding_options.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Funding Options","grader_hint":"Recalculate each option using the supplied fee, contribution, capacity, and budget terms; allow ±£1 for currency outputs."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommended funding option is one of the supplied options, satisfies every stated United Kingdom requirement, and is supported by the comparison rather than by an unsupported assertion.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"sandpiper_funding_options.docx; uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Funding Options; Redcliffe_cyber_compliance_assessment.docx","grader_hint":"Check the option against every requirement in the funding brief and verify that the recommendation follows the displayed comparison."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The compliance conclusion addresses each applicable requirement in the supplied United Kingdom policy basis and does not claim compliance for an unsupported requirement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx; Redcliffe_cyber_compliance_assessment.docx","grader_hint":"Make a checklist from the supplied policy basis and locate a supported status and evidence reference for every item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The defect log covers the mixed date representations, the notes-based row exceptions, and the stale retired helper column, with each defect tied to an affected field or record.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Defect Log","grader_hint":"Compare the seeded source conditions with the defect log and require a distinct affected-field or record reference for each category."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The defect log explains the budget or compliance impact of each material defect and distinguishes a supported correction from an assumption or unresolved limitation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Defect Log","grader_hint":"Review each logged issue for both an impact statement and an explicit evidence-versus-assumption disposition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The method identifies the review as limited to the United Kingdom requirements and evidence applicable on 30 September 2028.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx: Method & Sources; Redcliffe_cyber_compliance_assessment.docx","grader_hint":"Search both deliverables for the stated jurisdiction and as-of date and compare them with the policy basis."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The deliverables make no unsupported factual claims, estimates, or invented policy requirements, and clearly label any remaining assumption.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All supplied references; Both submitted deliverables","grader_hint":"A reviewer should trace substantive claims to a supplied reference or see them explicitly labelled as assumptions or limitations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Accepted lines, exclusions, corrections, and the recommendation carry enough source or record references for another analyst to reproduce the review.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Both submitted deliverables; All supplied references","grader_hint":"Inspect line-level or grouped source references and verify that they point to identifiable supplied files, sheets, records, or sections."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook presents corrected values rather than propagating the draft’s stale helper results or draft-only totals.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx; uk_policy_basis_2028.docx; Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx","grader_hint":"Compare the review’s accepted amounts and totals with the authoritative schedule/rate evidence and the retired helper values."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Neither submitted deliverable contains `#REF!`, `#DIV/0!`, `#VALUE!`, or equivalent broken-formula output.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Both submitted deliverables","grader_hint":"Inspect spreadsheet formulas and cached values and search extracted Word text for the listed error strings."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook’s displayed line values, subtotals, and totals are mutually consistent and do not rely on an undisclosed stale calculated field.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx","grader_hint":"Re-add visible line items, charges, and option components and compare them to displayed subtotals and totals with ±£1 currency tolerance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The workbook is usable as a public-facing decision document: labels are understandable, currency and dates are consistently presented, and the recommendation can be found without inspecting formulas.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx","grader_hint":"Render the workbook and assess whether an external decision maker can identify scope, corrected total, defects, options, and recommendation without reverse-engineering the file."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Word assessment contains the headings `Executive Recommendation`, `Scope and Evidence`, `Reconciliation`, `Quality Issues`, `Funding Options`, and `Assumptions and Limitations`.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Redcliffe_cyber_compliance_assessment.docx","grader_hint":"Extract paragraph styles and text and confirm all six exact headings appear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment’s corrected United Kingdom total, option comparison values, selected option, scope, and material defect conclusions agree with the workbook within ±£1 for currency figures.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":true,"evidence":"Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx; Redcliffe_cyber_compliance_assessment.docx","grader_hint":"Extract shared figures and conclusions from both deliverables and compare them directly; allow ±£1 for currency rounding."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The assessment is concise and decision-ready, explaining why the recommendation follows from the evidence while preserving material limitations instead of presenting false certainty.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Redcliffe_cyber_compliance_assessment.docx; All supplied references","grader_hint":"Render the document, confirm it is no longer than five pages, and judge whether a client decision maker can understand the conclusion, basis, and limitations."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Hedda Ferreira is reviewing Redcliffe Manufacturing’s completed cyber-insurance budget for Sandpiper Advisory before an external decision maker approves a funding route. The work is a focused inspection of one United Kingdom insurance programme against supplied policy, schedule, rate, and funding evidence.","difficulty_sources":["Normalising case and trailing-space differences before applying the supplied de-duplication key.","Resolving one ambiguous slash-form transaction date against executed schedule evidence.","Applying Notes-based row exceptions without allowing them to override unrelated fields.","Separating duplicate premiums from legitimate overlapping coverage layers.","Ignoring stale values in a retired helper column while reconciling the corrected budget.","Keeping two public-facing deliverables consistent on totals, option comparison, and recommendation."],"authoring_plan":{"source_count_target":5,"key_derivation":"reference_script","source_layout":{"redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx":{"role":"Existing completed workbook with a transaction register and draft budget calculations.","semantic_content":["Include a single Redcliffe programme with several United Kingdom coverage records and one clearly non-United-Kingdom record.","Use entity identifiers with case and trailing-space differences, including variants of the same synthetic identifier.","Include separate legitimate layers sharing a resolved date, plus one same-key duplicate import.","Use a transaction-date column containing ISO dates, an unambiguous day-first slash date, and one ambiguous slash date whose correct interpretation can be corroborated by the executed schedule.","Include a free-text Notes column with approved row-level exceptions: one supported premium override, one cancellation/exclusion instruction, and one instruction that the United Kingdom charge field is not applicable and must remain blank.","Include a clearly labelled retired helper column with stale values that disagree with authoritative evidence and must not be used."],"defects_exactly_seeded":["Mixed date and time representations in one transaction-date column, with one ambiguous slash-form value.","Per-row exceptions in free-text Notes that override the main columns.","Retired helper column containing stale values."],"cleanliness_constraints":["Do not add formula errors, missing source records, unexplained nulls, corrupted files, duplicate defect types, or unrelated layout traps.","Keep the source workbook readable and internally coherent apart from the three required layout defects."]},"uk_policy_basis_2028.docx":{"role":"Genuine internal governance note supplied by Redcliffe.","must_state":["The review scope is United Kingdom policy costs applicable on 30 September 2028.","The de-duplication key is normalised entity identifier, coverage layer, policy year, and resolved transaction date.","Entity identifiers are compared after trimming surrounding whitespace and applying case-insensitive matching.","Distinct coverage layers are legitimate separate premiums; only matching business keys are duplicates.","The evidence precedence is executed coverage schedule and approved endorsement evidence, then the frozen rate card, then draft workbook figures; the retired helper is non-authoritative.","An approved exception in Notes overrides only the named field or disposition.","An ambiguous date may be resolved only where corroborated by the executed schedule; the treatment must be disclosed.","The United Kingdom charge is blank where the supplied exception says it is not applicable; no estimate is permitted.","The assessment must address the supplied United Kingdom compliance fields without extending beyond the supplied policy text."]},"uk_cyber_rate_card_2028.xlsx":{"role":"Frozen rate-card snapshot, not a live source.","must_contain":["Synthetic layer codes and limit bands matching the schedule.","Rates or quoted premium bases sufficient to recalculate every accepted premium.","The applicable United Kingdom charge rate and the designated non-applicable exception treatment.","A stated effective period covering the required as-of date."],"numeric_design":"Use invented currency amounts, limits, and rates unrelated to any number in the prompt. Make the canonical line premiums reproducible to the penny or whole-pound level and make the endorsed exception agree with the executed evidence."},"redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx":{"role":"Executed schedule and endorsement evidence.","must_contain":["Synthetic Redcliffe entity identifiers, policy year, coverage layers, effective or transaction dates, United Kingdom scope, and authoritative premiums.","A schedule date that uniquely corroborates the ambiguous slash-form date in the draft.","At least one pair of distinct layers on an overlapping date and one same-key duplicate situation.","An approved endorsement corresponding to the premium override note.","A cancellation or other supported exclusion corresponding to the Notes exception.","A designated United Kingdom charge exemption corresponding to the intentional blank field."]},"sandpiper_funding_options.docx":{"role":"Funding-option brief from Sandpiper Advisory.","must_contain":["At least three named funding options with invented fees or costs, capacity, coverage consequences, and United Kingdom compliance conditions.","One option that is the defensible recommendation after the corrected budget is calculated.","At least one superficially cheaper option that fails a stated requirement and one compliant alternative with a different cost, so the recommendation requires comparison rather than simple copying.","All values must be frozen and text-extractable."]}},"reference_solution":{"method":"Use a Python reference script to read the supplied workbook and office documents, normalise identifiers, resolve the corroborated date, apply the policy precedence, process each approved Notes exception, retain distinct layers, exclude non-UK and cancelled records, calculate accepted premiums and charges from the frozen rate card, and evaluate every funding option against the supplied conditions.","outputs":["Generate a canonical workbook with the required sheets and transparent source references.","Generate a Word assessment using the required headings and the same canonical totals, option comparison, recommendation, and defect conclusions."],"verification":["Recalculate every accepted line and total independently from the source data.","Check that the designated charge-exempt field remains blank.","Check that no retired helper value influences any output.","Run the full 34-item rubric against the generated reference solution.","Render both deliverables and perform a human usability review."]}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"draft_budget","filename":"redcliffe_draft_budget.xlsx","purpose":"Completed but unreviewed cyber-insurance budget workbook containing the transaction register, embedded draft calculations, and the source evidence referenced by the finance team.","required":true,"discovery":"Open this first to understand the existing budget and locate the transaction-level records that require review."},{"artifact_id":"policy_basis","filename":"uk_policy_basis_2028.docx","purpose":"Internal policy and governance note stating the applicable United Kingdom review scope, evidence precedence, business key, treatment of approved row exceptions, and presentation requirements.","required":true,"discovery":"Use this with the coverage schedule to determine which source facts govern conflicting draft figures."},{"artifact_id":"rate_card","filename":"uk_cyber_rate_card_2028.xlsx","purpose":"Frozen United Kingdom cyber-insurance rate-card snapshot applicable to the stated as-of date, including layer, limit-band, premium, and tax or charge information.","required":true,"discovery":"Use it to validate accepted premiums and calculate the applicable United Kingdom charges; it is not a live internet source."},{"artifact_id":"coverage_schedule","filename":"redcliffe_coverage_schedule.docx","purpose":"Executed coverage schedule and endorsement evidence identifying Redcliffe entities, policy periods, coverage layers, United Kingdom applicability, and authoritative endorsed amounts.","required":true,"discovery":"Use it to corroborate transaction dates, distinguish genuine coverage layers from duplicate imports, and support corrections."},{"artifact_id":"funding_options","filename":"sandpiper_funding_options.docx","purpose":"Funding-option brief from Sandpiper Advisory listing the available options, costs, capacity, constraints, and United Kingdom compliance conditions.","required":true,"discovery":"Use it to build the comparison and select the option that can be recommended on the corrected evidence."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"review_workbook","filename":"Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"Corrected, public-facing cyber-insurance budget workbook with reconciled United Kingdom figures, defect log, method and sources, and funding-option comparison.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file at the top level of the starting working directory.","Include sheets named Budget Review, Defect Log, Method & Sources, and Funding Options.","Show traceable source references and retain no spreadsheet error values.","Do not use the retired helper column as a calculation basis."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"compliance_assessment","filename":"Redcliffe_cyber_compliance_assessment.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"External-facing compliance assessment explaining the reconciliation, quality issues, funding comparison, recommendation, and limitations.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file at the top level of the starting working directory.","Use the headings Executive Recommendation, Scope and Evidence, Reconciliation, Quality Issues, Funding Options, and Assumptions and Limitations.","Keep the document to five pages or fewer.","All shared figures and conclusions must agree with the workbook."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"inspect_quality","work_product":"compliance_assessment","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"supplied_source@v4","occupation":"financial_managers","sector":"finance_insurance","task_archetype":"supplied_source","estimated_professional_hours":5.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"reference_script","reviewer_policy":"A reference script derives the canonical figures from the supplied files, followed by an independent document and rendering review for source traceability, cross-deliverable agreement, compliance coverage, and public-facing usability.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The task is limited to the supplied United Kingdom policy text and frozen rate-card snapshot; it is not a live legal or insurance-market opinion.","Office rendering may vary slightly by spreadsheet or Word implementation, but all graded facts are text-extractable."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:36:24+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:36:24+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:36:24+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:36:24+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/1268c961dc837704","declared_deliverables":["Redcliffe_cyber_budget_review.xlsx","Redcliffe_cyber_compliance_assessment.docx"]};
